In the study presented here, a functional relevance of TTC30A–PRKACA interaction was shown, confirming the involvement of TTC30A in Shh signaling. We demonstrated that the loss or A375V mutant TTC30A has an impact on Smo localization and the phosphorylation of PKA substrates. Such a strong Shh phenotype would lead to embryonic lethality, indicating that synpolydactyly seen in patients carrying the A375V mutation reflects a subtle symptom based on TTC30B mutation.
